A||N||15||Bigfieroman||Problems w/parents?||||1||
Z||000000||Bigfieroman||01-07-2001||06:16 PM||||My parents helped me to buy my fiero in september by cashing in their ready-access CD to par the difference, and I must pay them back.  Well, I owe about $2000 now, and I just found an 88' GT with half the miles for a good price compared to what i can sell my car for.  Now, my parents have automatically said NO, no further discussion, because they told me to shou around more when i bought.  Any suggestions on what I should do?  I don't want to have to spend $$$ on a brake upgrade and a bump steer kit and a tranny conversion.  Please help me with advice!<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||01-07-2001||06:59 PM||||the fact that they paid so much the first time is way more than my parents could have done for me. just go with what you have, scale down your mod list and maybe upgrade to an '88 or more serious mods in the future when you can better afford to. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||01-07-2001||07:40 PM||||Keep in mind that you don't HAVE to spend money on a brake upgrade and bump steer kit, etc.  I ran my stock 85 SE 4 cyl 5sp at the last RFTH5 at Deals Gap, NC and was able to very comfortably keep up with the 88's and modified car on the incredible curves of Deals Gap.<P>Keep in mind the 88's will come with their own issues.  I used to have a Formula but sold it last spring.  While it did handle a little better than the earlier models, I got tired of struggling to find suspension and brake parts and paying twice as much compared to the 84-87 cars.  I recently picked up 2 87 GT's and I am much happier working on the old style suspension.<P>Enjoy what you have.  Parts are easy to find and I think you need to push the car close to it's limits to really see the differences in handling.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||01-07-2001||08:10 PM||||I totally agree with Bob's advice.  For now just try to get your parents paid back.  After that youcan start putting money aside for either your list of mods, or an 88.  There are going to be more good condition 88's around so Even if you had to wait a year or two I am certain you will find one.  But if your budget is that tight, I don't think you want to get into the 88's just yet.<P>I did my rear brakes last summer.  I am no expert on suspension stuff and decided to stay away from the different caliper design on the 88's.  I didn't have the special tools and didn't want to try doing it without them.  I took it to my mechanic, who does a great job and is almost always cheap.  He's one of the few people who I trust with my Fiero if I run into a problem I cannpot tackle by myself.  Well, he said he couldn't do it below $800, which included new rotors and calipers.  Well, needless to say thats a bit much for brakes, but I can understand since a lot of it was parts cost.  I ended up rebuilding both calipers myself and re-using the old rotors which were in very good condition.  Still, by the time I was done I was out about $150!!!  I just want you to know what your getting into with the 88's before you buy.  Good luck on whatever you choose!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||01-07-2001||08:47 PM||||Heck if you don't move on the 88' could you pass the info along to me....||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||01-07-2001||09:02 PM||||You can get rotors for the rears of '88s at Auto Zone for 15 bucks a piece.  For more info. use the search function...<P>I like the '88s because of way less bump steer, which is a BIG difference between the 2 suspensions.  <P>My old Formula handled great, KYB's all around and new bushings,  however, it wasn't as heavy as my current '88 GT, and it handled considerably better then the 4 pre-88s I have driven.  My current '88 has worn out bushings and shocks/struts, so its not handling too well. <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||4
Z||000006||Old Lar||01-07-2001||09:33 PM||||Some of us don't have our mommies and daddies around to help us buy cars.  It sounds like you have it pretty good and they went along with your decision to buy your first Fiero, now this one is not "good enough".  Time to grow up, get a job, then you can spend your money any way you want, rather than to tap your parents CDs.||||reg||3
Z||000007||Bigfieroman||01-07-2001||10:02 PM||||Go F$%K yourself, I have 2 jobs, and an allowence.  Don't make me out to be some slacker punk.  Plenty of kids at my school were GIVEN new cars for their birthdays.<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierofreek2001||01-07-2001||10:34 PM||||i know how it feels man, im 19 myself, and ive been wanting an 88 gt white with tan interior and t tops, and i found one for cheap one time, but i just cant afford it right now, even tho i work my @$$ off, but i do enjoy workin on my car, so hey, just fix the one up u have, and u can still turn heads....||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||01-07-2001||10:37 PM||||Ouch! The bullets are flyin now! <P>My feeling is that the question is not are 88's beter, rather then is it appropriate to go get a different car before you pay back what is borrowed from the folks. I don't think that is right. Neither is it right to make you out to be a snot nosed punk because your parents helped in the buying process. I am in my early 30's, married, and still I may find it necessary to turn to my folks for some type of support.<P>That being said, your folks are not the bank. While a bank don't care what you do as long as they get theirs, parents want their kids to learn from the mistakes made from impatience. Easy solution.Pay off the folks and move up on your own when the situations arise.  It certainly would do you no benefit to cause hard feelings at home by selling your car and buying an 88 that may be a total POS, then borrowing more money to fix it.<P>(Oh, and when faced with snide comments, show more class then going directly to the F yourself line. I know you got in in you, sport.)<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cheever2||01-07-2001||10:38 PM||||I don't mean for my advice to sound like "grow up", but the honest truth is: we ALL know of a nicer Fiero that we really want and can't quite seem to be able to obtain.  You just hopped into the same boat with the rest of us.  Give it a little time, enjoy what you have.  You'll get there.  Meanwhile, have fun Fiero'ing the best you can.  I support your eagerness to have better, but not much we can tell you that will help, as we have the same problem.  The Fieros are always shinier and faster on the other side of the fence, you know?  Hang in there.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000011||BAM-BAM||01-07-2001||11:08 PM||||  BFM, Chill bro, you're getting you hackles up for nothing. Stimpy said it best. You owe your parents first. Once that is taken care of, you can save a little and sell your car and buy what you want. I am about as impatient as they come and I have learned alot doing this Fiero thing. The biggest thing I have learned is that for every great deal you see today, there will be an even better one just down the road. Patients my friend, all in good time. Also, if you don't want to be taken as a slacker punk, cool it with the punk attitude. No one here is against you, albeit some of us can be testy and opinionated at times (right Stimp?). Anywho, chill, take a deep breath and set your priorities. Your time will come young Skywalker.<P>  Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||12
