Z||000014||streetracer||01-08-2001||02:50 AM||||i say stay with the car you have i got an 87 gt that i run circles around most of the cars in my area (on the street of course). most people will never be able to use the steering and the suspension upgrade from an 88 just because they will not be on their car that hard. if your worried about street racing and winning just go to a big open parking lot away from that cop and push your car to its limits to get the feel for it||||reg||1
Z||000015||Bigfieroman||01-08-2001||01:08 PM||||Ok, ok, fine.  Ill just upgrade my car.  I already have some 16" w/tires, and stainles brake lines.  From the sound of it, with a rear sway bar, a bump steer kit, and the brake upgrade, the car will be as good as, if not better than the 88's...also if maybe i remove the steering damper.  Thanks anyways guys.  <P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
